60407023248/https://looksmax.org/threads/why-hgh-is-cope-and-will-not-work-for-you-hgh-users-gtfih.1887337/"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"Ask HN: Anyone else in constant anxiety and how do you cope?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=21619671","site":"Hacker News","score":98,"comments":134,"year":2019},{"title":"Lego MRI Scanners donated to hospitals to help children cope with anxiety (2022)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37830599","site":"Hacker News","score":129,"comments":67,"year":2023}],"web":[{"title":"Incel (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Incel"},{"title":"Looksmaxxing (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Looksmaxxing"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Confidence & presence","chain":["Label a method as self-deception","Rank which methods get attention","Shapes what people try for looks"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Forum users apply 'cope' to sort looksmaxxing methods into those they consider real and those they consider wishful, which shapes what people end up trying for their looks. Blackpill users also apply it to self-improvement itself. It is slang for argument, not a technique."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["'Cope' (and its jokey form 'copium') is online slang used in blackpill, incel and looksmaxxing communities to dismiss a method, belief or argument as a self-deceptive way of coping with an unwelcome reality. [1][2]","Grokipedia says the term is applied to optimistic views and self-improvement efforts that adherents consider delusional, and that blackpill adherents use it to dismiss personality and behaviour as ineffective. [1] In looksmaxxing, it is also used to rank low-rated methods, such as thumbpulling, on tier lists. [2]","No academic studies of the word itself were found. Research on the surrounding communities is cited below."],"infobox":[["Type","Community slang"],["Used in","Incel, blackpill and looksmaxxing forums"],["Related terms","Blackpill, LDAR, mogging"]],"sections":[{"h":"Usage","paras":["In incel and blackpill discourse, 'cope' labels optimism or self-improvement as self-deception, and a believer might call anything from a personality-based strategy to a skincare routine 'cope'. [1]","In looksmaxxing, Grokipedia describes the term as dismissing a method as ineffective or self-deceptive, and gives thumbpulling as an example that tier lists rank low. [2]","Users also apply it to themselves. One looksmax.org poster describes telling themselves they look better as 'cope' that collapses periodically, illustrating how the word can describe both external arguments and internal reassurance."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Research and expert views","paras":["Grokipedia notes that the fatalism behind much 'cope' language rests on evolutionary and dating-data arguments that it says overgeneralise short-term mating research. [1] A 2025 sociological analysis of a looksmaxxing forum examined how its users critique bodies and frame self-improvement, which relates to how methods are ranked and dismissed."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Incel (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Incel","source":"Grokipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Looksmaxxing (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Looksmaxxing","source":"Grokipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Coping w philtrum of death","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/coping-w-philtrum-of-death.1716117/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218144107/https://looksmax.org/threads/coping-w-philtrum-of-death.1716117/"},{"title":"Cope with bullying","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/cope-with-bullying.1681886/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251215231927/https://looksmax.org/threads/cope-with-bullying.1681886/"},{"title":"Cope looksmaxing methods (and why)","url":"https://looksmax.o